<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Larnaca</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Larnaca is a port city on the south coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a>, built over ancient Kition. Kition was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/late-bronze-age">Late Bronze Age</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a>-working town, then a Phoenician city-kingdom from the 9th century BCE and the birthplace of Zeno, founder of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stoicism">Stoicism</a>. Under Ottoman rule Larnaca was the island's main port and home of the European consuls, and today it has Cyprus's main international airport.</p></div>
